Address over and under consumption   
’Nudges’ to consumers; product labelling; local reuse or fix-up initiatives; corporate or NGO led initiatives to discourage overbuying; taxes on consumption; consumer reduced-consumption movements  
Expansion of sharing economy; transition towns; sufficiency orientation of consumers; design for sustainability for products and services
 
Beliefs in rationality of markets; dogma of consumer sovereignty; lack of policies that address leakage & telecoupling; political risks for tax increases; potentials for consumer backlashes
 Citizens; private sector; national governments; NGOs; scientific groups
 National and local 
